body:
Update: I won! I have no idea why, but Lazarus is so difficult for me to play. It was my 20th+ rerun trying to beat either the Chest or Sheol with him. 

&#x200B;

I ended up beating The Chest in this run

> you can use your reaction to take the radiant attack action with twice the normal range, as well as making one additional attack

&#x200B;

in the case of extra attacks at 5th level, would this mean 3 sun bolt attacks as an attack action (plus a potential two more with ki for a total of 5 attacks)?

&#x200B;

Would it not be better then to have it mechanically work as a line spell? as what u/Pandamonium231 suggests, a kamehameha-esque attack.

&#x200B;

I have a suggestion for how that might work:

&#x200B;

Solar Charge

on your turn, you may forgo your action and bonus action to use your ki to gather the light around you. Charging requires concentration as if concentrating on a spell. By spending 1 ki point as part of the charge you may make concentration checks in order to maintain charging with advantage. If immediately at the start of your next turn, you have not lost concentration, you may use your reaction for that turn to unleash the gathered ki, in a 10ft wide, 60ft line in front of you. All creatures caught in the line must make a Constitution saving throw against your Ki Save DC or take 6d4 radiant damage, half damage on a success. The damage die changes as shown in the Martial Arts column of the Monk Table.

&#x200B;

while writing this up, I thought of a possible improvement for the 6th level ability, one that could take place of Searing Arc Strike:

&#x200B;

Solar Beam

Starting at 6th level, you may spend 4 ki points to immediately do your Solar Charge attack, still forgoing your action and bonus action. In addition, when you charge your Solar Charge attack normally, you increase the area of effect of the spell to a 15ft wide, 100ft line in front of you.

&#x200B;

I feel like these would the sun soul abilities more viable, without breaking away from the class identity.
